                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16611703" author="klaster_1" created="Wed, 12 Sep 2018 07:38:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The issue happens because &lt;em&gt;AgentManager&lt;/em&gt; class name property gets changed to &lt;em&gt;AgentManager_service_AgentManager&lt;/em&gt; as a part of scope hoisting by &lt;em&gt;ModuleConcatenationPlugin&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Relevant issues:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/webpack-contrib/uglifyjs-webpack-plugin/issues/234&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/webpack-contrib/uglifyjs-webpack-plugin/issues/234&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/5463&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/5463&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Out options are:&lt;br/&gt;
1. Don&apos;t rely on class and function names for DI. I prefer this one because in the end we&apos;ll be using strings as DI tokens, which is the canonical AngularJS approach.&lt;br/&gt;
2. Disable &lt;em&gt;ModuleConcatenationPlugin&lt;/em&gt;. This will probably increase production bundle size, not a good idea.&lt;br/&gt;
3. Try &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/webpack-contrib/uglifyjs-webpack-plugin/issues/234#issuecomment-369134047&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;this approach&lt;/a&gt;. It introduces unnecessary webpack config compication, so I don&apos;t like it.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=anovikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;anovikov&quot;&gt;anovikov&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=kuaw26&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;kuaw26&quot;&gt;kuaw26&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alexdel&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alexdel&quot;&gt;alexdel&lt;/a&gt; what do you think?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16611710" author="klaster_1" created="Wed, 12 Sep 2018 07:45:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=kuaw26&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;kuaw26&quot;&gt;kuaw26&lt;/a&gt; please review. I chose the first option and replaced DI tokens with strings everywhere.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16611711" author="klaster_1" created="Wed, 12 Sep 2018 07:46:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;By the way, I&apos;ve updated Babel 7 (and some related dependencies) to the latest version.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16612054" author="kuaw26" created="Wed, 12 Sep 2018 12:32:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks good to me.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pkonstantinov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pkonstantinov&quot;&gt;pkonstantinov&lt;/a&gt;, Please test in branch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To test - just do a smoke test that most of screens work without any errors in console.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Only Web Console build was changed.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16613106" author="alexdel" created="Thu, 13 Sep 2018 07:01:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;cite&gt;The issue happens because&#160;&lt;em&gt;AgentManager&lt;/em&gt;&#160;class name property gets changed to&#160;&lt;em&gt;AgentManager_service_AgentManager&lt;/em&gt;&#160;as a part of scope hoisting by&#160;&lt;em&gt;ModuleConcatenationPlugin&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;cite&gt;Relevant issues:&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;cite&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/webpack-contrib/uglifyjs-webpack-plugin/issues/234&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/webpack-contrib/uglifyjs-webpack-plugin/issues/234&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;cite&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/5463&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/5463&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;cite&gt;Out options are:&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;cite&gt;1. Don&apos;t rely on class and function names for DI. I prefer this one because in the end we&apos;ll be using strings as DI tokens, which is the canonical AngularJS approach.&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;cite&gt;2. Disable&#160;&lt;em&gt;ModuleConcatenationPlugin&lt;/em&gt;. This will probably increase production bundle size, not a good idea.&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;cite&gt;3. Try&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/webpack-contrib/uglifyjs-webpack-plugin/issues/234#issuecomment-369134047&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;this approach&lt;/a&gt;. It introduces unnecessary webpack config compication, so I don&apos;t like it.&lt;/cite&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I suppose the first approach is the most suitable. By the way do we have any angularjs parts that don&apos;t use string tokens based DI?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16613140" author="pkonstantinov" created="Thu, 13 Sep 2018 07:41:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;A smoke test is done. No problems found.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16613161" author="klaster_1" created="Thu, 13 Sep 2018 07:57:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alexdel&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alexdel&quot;&gt;alexdel&lt;/a&gt; not in AngularJS, but Angular can use either a string or a class.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16613235" author="kuaw26" created="Thu, 13 Sep 2018 09:19:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged to master.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=pkonstantinov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;pkonstantinov&quot;&gt;pkonstantinov&lt;/a&gt;, please do smoke test in master and close this issue.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
